 # DICOM Volume Loading and Coordinate Reconstruction
 
-Also called: DICOM File Loading and Stacking, DICOM Loader, DICOM Volume Reconstruction Loading & Density Conversion, DICOM to Density Conversion, Volume DICOM Loading and Rescaling
+Also called: DICOM File Loading and Stacking, DICOM Loader, DICOM Volume Loading and Normalization, DICOM Volume Reconstruction Loading & Density Conversion, DICOM to Density Conversion, Volume DICOM Loading and Rescaling
 
 ## Overview
-This method loads a 3D volumetric dataset from a series of DICOM image files, reconstructs the physical voxel grid by resolving coordinate system conventions, and converts raw pixel values into physical density [S2, unofficial]. It specifically addresses the discrepancy between DICOM's pixel-center coordinate convention and the corner-point convention required by downstream volume rendering engines, while handling the non-cubic nature of medical voxels [S1, unofficial]. It differs from generic volume loaders by explicitly managing DICOM-specific metadata (Rescale Slope/Intercept, Pixel Spacing, Slice Thickness) and orientation flips (rot90) necessary for correct anatomical alignment [S2, S3, unofficial].
+This method loads a 3D volume from a series of DICOM slice files, converts raw pixel values to physical density (Hounsfield Units normalized to water = 1.0), and reconstructs the correct voxel partition by accounting for DICOM coordinate conventions and spacing [S2, S3, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from generic loaders by explicitly handling the conversion from DICOM's middle-of-pixel coordinate system to the corner-point convention required by many rendering engines (e.g., ODL), and by normalizing density relative to water rather than just scaling to [0, 1] [S2, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-**Inputs:** A directory of DICOM files (typically `.dcm` or `.IMA`), sorted by filename [S2, unofficial].
-**Outputs:** A 3D density array (float), a physical bounding box (min/max points), and voxel dimensions (scale) [S2, S3, unofficial].
