 ### DICOM Volume Texture Preparation
-This variant prepares the loaded volume for GPU rendering by quantizing the continuous density values into a discrete window range (defined by lower and upper Hounsfield unit thresholds) and integer-downsampling the texture if any axis exceeds 256 voxels [S1, unofficial]. It stores the physical size of the volume in millimeters separately from the texture dimensions to preserve anisotropic scaling information during the downsampling process [S1, unofficial].
